Z||000000||LAMBO||09-21-2000||05:22 PM||||For those of you who haven't had to work on your babies for awhile, heres some pictorial reminders of all the FUN you're missing.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/motor1.JPG"> <BR>Donor motor almost ready to go in.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/motor2.JPG"> <BR>Old motor with broken timeing chain.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/motor3.JPG"> <BR>Donor motor car. What do I do with it now?<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/motor4.JPG"> <BR>New exhaust. Notice something missing? (I don't mean the tips either.)<BR>Should be running in a couple days.<BR>Lambo<P>||||reg||12
Z||000001||DaRkLoRD||09-21-2000||07:05 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by LAMBO:<BR><B>Donor motor car. What do I do with it now?<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Ok.. here's what you do..<P>get a really really big cardboard box.. put the Fiero inside it.. stick about 10lbs of stamps on it.. get a really big black marker and write on the side:<P>Fiero Project<BR>c/o Steve King<BR>85....<P>ah nevermind. it was worth a try.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||10
Z||000002||whamel||09-21-2000||08:15 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by LAMBO:<BR><B><BR>Donor motor car. What do I do with it now?<BR> </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You could finish installing that bike it looks like you're test fitting.  I'm not sure what kind of adapter you'd need, but I'm sure we can figure one out.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  Probably get great MPG and be good exercise too!||||reg||1
Z||000003||HugGRRRFiero||09-21-2000||08:25 PM||||Lambo, here's a couple ideas I remember seeing on the Red Green Show for that donor car.<P>First, bolt the bad engine & cradle back in and get the car rolling again.  Take all of the windows out of it, part it out if you wish but leave the seats in it.  Take the car or frame or whatever is left and roll it into the woods and find a good spot for it.  You could use it to make a comfortable deer blind.<P>Another idea, you could roll it out into the corner of your front yard and put plants all over it.  Put some plants and vines all over the car, any variety you choose.  Put some flowers all around the base of the car.  Leave the windows in it so you can use the inside as a greenhouse to store your plants in the winter.  Remove the spare tire and use the space for a rolled up garden hose.  The empty headlight bucket areas work great for storing little shovels and what not.  Store your rakes, hoes, and your peatmoss in the rear trunk.  Leave the hood and deck lid and doors on it so you can lock up your garden supplies, keep them out of the weather, and they will be right there with the car whenever you need to use them.  What you'll have is a attractive looking year round flower and garden center that you, or girlfriend, or wife, and maybe your neighbors will love for many long years.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>          <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/huggrrr.gif">        <BR>        <A HREF="mailto:HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com">HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||3
Z||000004||bHooper||09-21-2000||08:38 PM||||ah... the good ole days.  the 4x4, the palette on wheels... backside of the car 4 ft in the air.<P>brings back fond memories of last spring, the birds chirping, the coolant spilling everywhere, whacking my head on the bottomside of the trunk, break fluid squirting everywhere.  <P>uh oh, whats that, it starting to give me a itch... where's my jackstands?  there must be some good reason to pull the engine... hmmm... yea.. that'll be a sure fire way to fix my serpentine belt problem!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000005||80's BOY||09-21-2000||09:14 PM||||that reminds me....i need to check my tranny fluid or this will be ME soon. my barn isn't that nice though. add gravel and fire ants then you've got frustration!!||||reg||7
Z||000006||coachreed||09-24-2000||10:57 PM||||OK, I hate to ask this question, but how do you get the back of the car that high in the air?  I am in the process of helping a friend remove, rebuild/replace, and reinstall the engine in his '86 2M4.  I have done my fair share of work, but this one has me thinking.  I would greatly appreciate an explanation on how you did this?  Where do you jack from?  Do you wait for the cradle to be on the ground before you lift the car that high?  Is it stable there with the car at that angle, sitting on a 4x4, sitting on jack stands?  Just have to know since I have way too many people in and out of my garage.<P>Thanks in advance.<P>------------------<BR>Coach... I mean Randy (I often forget who I really am)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/coach_reed.geo" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/coach_reed.geo/images/coachbanner.jpg"> </A><BR>*<A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/coach_reed.geo" TARGET=_blank><B>The Red Bullet Web Page</B></A>* <A HREF="mailto:rreed5@home.com">rreed5@home.com</A> *<A HREF="http://www.ls1fun.com" TARGET=_blank>LS1Fun.com</A>*<A HREF="http://www.bodyformdesigns.com" TARGET=_blank>Body Form Designs</A>*<A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/coach_reed.geo/dynosrca.html" TARGET=_blank>Dyno</A>*||||reg||1
Z||000007||wkayl||09-24-2000||11:45 PM||||When I removed the engine from my son's 84SE, I just removed the rear taillights and bumper.  That left the metal "frame" exposed to hook a chain hoist to.  It worked great to lift the rear of the car.||||reg||1
